  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7pg6Q_",
      "title": "Karst gas-limit reset — Unichain Mainnet (060)",
      "author": "sbvegan",
      "number": 1482,
      "body": "## Context\n\nKarst (U19) has an op-node/kona-node bug that leaves the effective L2 block gas limit ~55 MGas above the value stored in the SystemConfig after the activation block (see Notion *\"P/PS: Karst Gas Limit Bug\"*). The approved mitigation is a per-chain **SystemConfig transaction** that re-emits the gas `ConfigUpdate`, resetting the effective gas limit back to the on-chain value.\n\nMainnet Karst activates **2026-07-08**. This task runs *after* activation.\n\n## What this adds\n\nReference task for **Unichain Mainnet** re-affirming the chain's current on-chain gas limit via `SystemConfig.setGasLimit`. Uses the `SystemConfigGasLimit` template (setGasLimit only — no EIP-1559 params).\n\n| Task | Chain | gasLimit |\n|---|---|---|\n| `060-gas-limit-unichain` | Unichain | 60M |\n\nUnichain's SystemConfig is owned by the **operator Safe** (`0x9245d5D10AA8a842B31530De71EA86c0760Ca1b1`), not the Foundation Upgrade Safe. This is a reference task for the operator to execute independently of the FUS. Nonce override is **9** (verify live nonce before signing).\n\n## Validation\n\nSimulates cleanly via `just simulate-stack eth 060-gas-limit-unichain`. The recorded hashes in `VALIDATION.md` are confirmed against simulation output.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Only `setGasLimit` is called (no `setEIP1559Params`) — the `SystemConfigGasLimit` template is used.\n- Unichain already has `gasLimit = 60000000` on chain; the call re-emits the `ConfigUpdate` event without changing storage.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-23T06:44:05Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
